"The steps below are for profiling on `x86_64`, running in `QEMU`. It is "
"possible to run the tests on real hardware, although retrieving the data "
"require additional effort."
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:59
msgid ""
"The profiling code is written primarily for QEMU, but for real hardware, "
"consider commenting out the `serio_command` code in the `src/profiling.rs` "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:61
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:63
msgid "Open a terminal window in the `redox` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:65
msgid "Install the tools:"
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:75
msgid ""
"Rename the `kernel = {}` item at `config/base.toml` to `profiling-kernel = {}"
"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:77
msgid ""
"In your first terminal window, from the `redox` directory, create the "
"filesystem configuration (`config/my_profiler.toml`, for example) or adapt "
"your existing configuration with the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:79
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"include = [ \"minimal.toml\" ]\n"
"\n"
"# General settings\n"
"[general]\n"
"# Filesystem size in MiB\n"
"filesystem_size = 256\n"
"\n"
"# Package settings\n"
"[packages]\n"
"# The kernel recipe with profiling code enabled\n"
"profiling-kernel = {}\n"
"# This is the profiling daemon\n"
"profiled = {}\n"
"# Add any other recipes you need for testing here\n"
"\n"
"# Init script to start the profile daemon\n"
"# The sequence number \"01\" ensures it will be started right after the "
"drivers\n"
"[[files]]\n"
"path = \"/usr/lib/init.d/01_profile\"\n"
"data = \"\"\"\n"
"profiled\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"[[files]]\n"
"path = \"/usr/bin/perf_tests.sh\"\n"
"data = \"\"\"\n"
"dd bs=4k count=100000 < /scheme/zero > /scheme/null\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"# Script to perform performance tests - add your tests here\n"
"# If you will be testing manually, you don't need this section\n"
"[[files]]\n"
"path = \"/usr/lib/init.d/99_tests\"\n"
"data = \"\"\"\n"
"echo Waiting for startup to complete...\n"
"sleep 5\n"
"echo\n"
"echo Running tests...\n"
"ion -x /usr/bin/perf_tests.sh\n"
"echo Shutting down...\n"
"shutdown\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/performance.md:124
msgid ""
"If you don't want to use the `99_tests` file configuration, you can use the "
"`kprof_record` command (can't be used in multiple commands) from `profiled` "
"recipe."
msgstr ""

